0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  B8Script interpreter for the Intel 8080
0000                             ;  Spec: docs/b8script.md (2026-10-09) plus the 2026-11-20 changes:
0000                             ;        [x stores in a variable, "[ " pushes an anonymous block, any other
0000                             ;        character after [ is an error, the heap pointer lives at z10+.
0000                             ;        The string escape is "/" (it was ">").
0000                             ;        Dividing by zero is not checked. -n? does no more editing than
0000                             ;        Backspace.
0000                             ;  Design follows the Z80 interpreter (z80/b8s-z80.asm), with 8080 opcodes
0000                             ;  only.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Two switches, set in the two EQU lines below:
0000                             ;    CPM      0 = generic ROM build (KEY/CONOUT at fixed addresses)
0000                             ;             1 = CP/M 2.2 .COM file: loads the file named on the command line
0000                             ;    CHECKED  0 = no checks (spec: "B8Script checks nothing")
0000                             ;             1 = stops on stack overrun, Ctrl-C, heap past the limit, a store
0000                             ;                 outside the program's own space, and a bad character after [,
0000                             ;                 printing a letter and the place, like  S @ 245
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Assembler: asm80 (https://maly.github.io/asm80-node/), I8080 mode.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                CPM:      EQU   1   ; 1 = CP/M .COM build
0000                CHECKED:   EQU   1   ; 1 = checked build
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Register use, everywhere in the interpreter
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    BC   IP: the address of the next program character to read
0000                             ;    HL   TOS: the top data-stack cell is kept here, not in memory
0000                             ;    SP   the data stack: (SP) is NOS, the cell under TOS. The data stack is
0000                             ;         the 8080"s own stack, which is what the spec"s machine-code contract
0000                             ;         needs ("the data cells above the return address").
0000                             ;    A DE scratch. Every handler is entered with HL = TOS and may use A, DE.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The return stack pointer has no register (the 8080 has no spare pair): it
0000                             ;  is the RAM word RSP. Only rpop, rpushd and ")" (and the checks) touch it.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  One-byte calls. The routines used most are reached with RST, one byte
0000                             ;  instead of three. (asm80 wants the vector number: RST 1 = RST 08h.)
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    RST 1  08h  rpop    pop the return stack into HL
0000                             ;    RST 3  18h  drop    drop TOS, then next character     (ends a handler)
0000                             ;    RST 4  20h  neg16   HL = -HL
0000                             ;    RST 5  28h  putc    print A
0000                             ;    RST 6  30h  next    next character                    (ends a handler)
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  RST 3 and RST 6 never return: an RST is a CALL, so the first thing each
0000                             ;  of them does is POP D to throw the return address away.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The CP/M build can't own page zero, so the block from `vecs` to `vecend`
0000                             ;  (image addresses 0108h-0133h) is copied to 0008h-0033h when it starts. The
0000                             ;  code in that block has no jumps inside itself, so it works at either place.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Dispatch. PTAB holds one byte per punctuation character: the low byte of
0000                             ;  its handler's address. The high byte is worked out from the character:
0000                             ;  the handlers of the first NPG1 characters (in code order) start in the
0000                             ;  image's second page, the rest in its first. The layout below keeps to
0000                             ;  that, and testing/chktab.py checks it in every build.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  What the 8080 lacks, and what replaces it: no JR (JMP/Jcc), no DJNZ, no
0000                             ;  SBC HL (byte-wise SUB/SBB, or negate and DAD), no shifts on register pairs
0000                             ;  (DAD H doubles; RAL/RAR through A), no LDIR/CPIR (small loops).
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Memory map. Everything the interpreter writes is in four RAM pages:
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    RSPAGE   return stack, 112 entries (the pointer stays inside this page)
0000                             ;    DSPAGE   data stack, 127 cells (SP stays inside this page)
0000                             ;    LETPAGE  letter cells: A..Z at +00h..+33h, a..z at +40h..+73h (so a word
0000                             ;             cell is always 64 bytes below its variable), the heap pointer at
0000                             ;             +7Ch (= z10+), interpreter variables in the gaps, and the -n?
0000                             ;             line buffer at +80h..+FFh
0000                             ;    PROG     the program text, NUL-terminated; the heap starts after the NUL
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The stacks sit below the letter page, so "the program's own space" (what
0000                             ;  the checked build lets ! and . write) is the single range from the letter
0000                             ;  page up to the heap limit. Each stack's page has a guard band: the data
0000                             ;  stack can overrun by a cell or two (and the calls made while it is full)
0000                             ;  into the top 32 bytes of the return-stack page, which are never used, and
0000                             ;  the return stack by one entry into the page below it.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                          IF   CPM   
0000                BDOS:     EQU   0005h   
0000                EXIT:     EQU   0000h   ; warm boot
0000                BASE:     EQU   0100h   ; where the image starts
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IFN   CPM   
                                 ; ---- generic machine: edit these to suit -----------------------------------
                    KEY:      EQU   0FF06h   ; a waiting key in A, or A = 0 if none is
                                 ;   waiting. The zero flag must match A
                                 ;   (end the routine with ORA A / RET).
                    CONOUT:   EQU   0FF03h   ; print the character in A
                    EXIT:     EQU   0FF09h   ; where to go when the program ends
                                 ;   KEY and CONOUT must preserve BC, DE and HL.
                    RSPAGE:   EQU   80h   ; 8000h return stack
                    DSPAGE:   EQU   81h   ; 8100h data stack
                    LETPAGE:   EQU   82h   ; 8200h letter cells and line buffer
                    PROG:     EQU   8300h   ; where the loader puts the program text
                    HEAPLIM:   EQU   0F0h   ; the heap must stay below F000h (a page)
                    BASE:     EQU   0000h   ; where the image starts
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                MSLOOP:   EQU   40   ; n? inner loop count for about 1 ms (1-255):
0000                             ; each pass calls getk once, so tune it for
0000                             ; your clock and your KEY routine
0000                             ; letter-page layout (offsets inside LETPAGE)
0000                LET:      EQU   LETPAGE*256   
0000                HEAP:     EQU   LET+7Ch   ; z10+, the heap pointer
0000                RSP:      EQU   LET+34h   ; gap after Z: the return stack pointer;
0000                KEYBUF:   EQU   LET+36h   ;   a held-back key
0000                LBHDR:    EQU   LET+7Eh   ; CP/M BDOS 10 header: max, count
0000                LINEBUF:   EQU   LET+80h   ; -n? text, ending in CR
0000                RSTOP:    EQU   RSPAGE*256+0E0h   ; empty return stack: the 32 bytes above it
0000                             ; take calls made while the data stack is full
0000                DSTOP:    EQU   DSPAGE*256+0FEh   ; empty data stack
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  The first 49 bytes: the entry, then the RST routines, with small handlers
0000                             ;  and routines filling the gaps between them. Generic: this IS page zero.
0000                             ;  CP/M: it is the start of the .COM file, and 0108h-0133h is also copied to
0000                             ;  page zero (see the header).
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0100                          .ORG   BASE   
0100   31 FE 06               LXI   SP,DSTOP   ; 00  reset, or the start of the .COM file
0103   C3 86 04               JMP   start   
0106   CF           RDROP:    RST   1   ; 06  drop the top of the return stack, then
0107   DF                     RST   3   ;     drop TOS (a spent flag) and go on
0108                VECS:        
0108                             ; ---- RST 1: rpop: pop the return stack into HL (DE is lost) -----------------
0108   2A 34 07     RPOP:     LHLD   RSP   ; 08
010B   5E                     MOV   E,M   
010C   23                     INX   H   
010D   56                     MOV   D,M   
010E   23                     INX   H   
010F   22 34 07               SHLD   RSP   
0112   EB                     XCHG      
0113   C9                     RET      ; 13  (so RST 2 is not used)
0114   EB           H_TOR:    XCHG      ; 14  "{" TOS to the return stack; rpushd
0115   C3 B4 01               JMP   rpushd   ;     brings up the new TOS
0118                             ; ---- RST 3: drop TOS, then next ---------------------------------------------
0118   D1           RST18:    POP   D   ; 18  discard the RST's return address
0119   E1                     POP   H   ;     new TOS = NOS
011A   C3 34 01               JMP   next0   
011D   E5           H_FROMR:   PUSH   H   ; 1D  "}" return stack to TOS
011E   CF                     RST   1   
011F   F7                     RST   6   
0120                             ; ---- RST 4: neg16: HL = -HL (keeps BC, DE) ----------------------------------
0120   AF           NEG16:    XRA   A   ; 20
0121   95                     SUB   L   
0122   6F                     MOV   L,A   
0123   9F                     SBB   A   
0124   94                     SUB   H   
0125   67                     MOV   H,A   
0126   C9                     RET      
0127   E9           JPHL:     PCHL      ; 27  (for the machine-code call)
0128                             ; ---- RST 5: putc: print A (keeps BC, DE, HL) --------------------------------
0128                RST28:       
0128                          IFN   CPM   
                    PUTC:     JMP   CONOUT   ; 28
0128                          ENDIF      
0128                          IF   CPM   
0128   C3 0D 04               JMP   putc   ; 28
012B                          ENDIF      
012B                             ; exec: "`" with no hex digit after it: call the machine code at TOS. It
012B                             ; returns here, with its top cell on the stack: that becomes the new TOS.
012B   CD 27 01     EXEC:     CALL   jphl   ; 2B
012E   E1                     POP   H   
012F   F7                     RST   6   
0130                             ; ---- RST 6: next character --------------------------------------------------
0130   D1           RST30:    POP   D   ; 30  discard the RST's return address
0131                          IF   CPM   
0131   C3 34 01               JMP   next0   ; (this copy runs in page zero)
0134                          ENDIF      
0134                VECEND:      
0134                             ; =============================================================================
0134                             ;  The inner loop: read one character and sort it by range.
0134                             ; 
0134                             ;    00h          end of program
0134                             ;    01h-20h, 7Fh-FFh   ignored (control, space, DEL, high bytes)
0134                             ;    30h-39h      digit: read a whole number
0134                             ;    41h-5Ah      A-Z: call the word in that letter's cell
0134                             ;    61h-7Ah      a-z: push the address of that letter's cell
0134                             ;    the rest     punctuation: jump through PTAB, 32 entries, in code order
0134                             ; =============================================================================
0134                NEXT0:       
0134                          IF   CHECKED   
0134   CD 1B 04               CALL   chkstk   ; both stacks are checked once per character
0137                          ENDIF      
0137   0A                     LDAX   B   
0138   03                     INX   B   
0139   D6 21                  SUI   21h   ; A = c - 21h
013B   DA 7B 01               JC   ctl   ; c < 21h: NUL ends, the rest are ignored
013E   FE 0F                  CPI   0Fh   
0140   DA 6B 01               JC   punct   ; 21h-2Fh: PTAB index 0-14
0143   D6 0F                  SUI   0Fh   ; A = c - 30h
0145   FE 0A                  CPI   0Ah   
0147   DA 53 03               JC   digit   ; 30h-39h
014A   FE 11                  CPI   11h   
014C   DA 69 01               JC   p3a   ; 3Ah-40h
014F   D6 11                  SUI   11h   ; A = c - 41h
0151   FE 1A                  CPI   1Ah   
0153   DA AA 01               JC   upper   ; 41h-5Ah: A = letter index 0-25
0156   FE 20                  CPI   20h   
0158   DA 67 01               JC   p5b   ; 5Bh-60h
015B   FE 3A                  CPI   3Ah   
015D   DA A4 01               JC   lower   ; 61h-7Ah: A = 20h-39h (cell +64 bytes)
0160   FE 3E                  CPI   3Eh   
0162   D2 34 01               JNC   next0   ; 7Fh-FFh: ignored
0165   D6 1A                  SUI   1Ah   ; 7Bh-7Eh: -1Eh in all, index 28-31
0167   D6 09        P5B:      SUI   9   ; 5Bh-60h: -4 in all, index 22-27
0169   C6 05        P3A:      ADI   5   ; 3Ah-40h: index 15-21
016B                             ; Punctuation: A = the PTAB index. The handler starts with HL = TOS,
016B                             ; untouched, and A, DE free.
016B   C6 33        PUNCT:    ADI   PTAB & 0FFh   ; PTAB never crosses a page
016D   5F                     MOV   E,A   
016E   16 03                  MVI   D,PTAB / 256   
0170   FE 49                  CPI   (PTAB & 0FFh) + NPG1   ; carry: one of the first NPG1
0172   1A                     LDAX   D   
0173   5F                     MOV   E,A   ; the handler's low byte
0174                          IFN   CPM   
                              MVI   A,0   
                              RAL      ; its page: 0 + carry
0174                          ENDIF      
0174                          IF   CPM   
0174   3E 01                  MVI   A,1   
0176   CE 00                  ACI   0   ; its page: 1 + carry
0178                          ENDIF      
0178   57                     MOV   D,A   
0179   D5                     PUSH   D   ; jump to it; the stack is balanced again
017A   C9                     RET      ;   when the handler starts
017B                             ; ctl: characters below 21h. A = c - 21h.
017B   C6 21        CTL:      ADI   21h   ; back to c; zero only for NUL
017D   C2 34 01               JNZ   next0   ; the rest are ignored
0180   C3 00 00     ENDPROG:   JMP   EXIT   ; the program has ended
0183                             ; =============================================================================
0183                             ;  Handlers that must start in the image's first page: ^ _ ` | ~
0183                             ;  (00bbIGFuZCA= are up among the RST routines.)
0183                             ; =============================================================================
0183   D1           H_XOR:    POP   D   
0184   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0185   AA                     XRA   D   
0186   67                     MOV   H,A   
0187   7D                     MOV   A,L   
0188   AB                     XRA   E   
0189   6F                     MOV   L,A   
018A   F7                     RST   6   
018B   D1           H_OR:     POP   D   
018C   7C                     MOV   A,H   
018D   B2                     ORA   D   
018E   67                     MOV   H,A   
018F   7D                     MOV   A,L   
0190   B3                     ORA   E   
0191   6F                     MOV   L,A   
0192   F7                     RST   6   
0193   E7           H_NOT:    RST   4   ; ~x = -x - 1
0194   2B                     DCX   H   
0195   F7                     RST   6   
0196                             ; "_" ( n -- addr ): the heap pointer moves up by n; TOS is the old pointer.
0196   EB           H_ALLOC:   XCHG      
0197   2A 7C 07               LHLD   HEAP   
019A   E5                     PUSH   H   
019B   19                     DAD   D   ; the new top
019C                          IF   CHECKED   
019C   CD 55 04               CALL   chkhp   
019F                          ENDIF      
019F   22 7C 07               SHLD   HEAP   
01A2   E1                     POP   H   
01A3   F7                     RST   6   
01A4                             ; ---- the letters and digits --------------------------------------------------
01A4                             ; a-z: push the cell's address (the cell is the variable)
01A4   E5           LOWER:    PUSH   H   
01A5   87                     ADD   A   
01A6   6F                     MOV   L,A   
01A7   26 07                  MVI   H,LETPAGE   
01A9   F7                     RST   6   
01AA                             ; A-Z: call the word. The return address (the IP after the letter) goes on
01AA                             ; the return stack, and the IP becomes the address in the letter's cell.
01AA   E5           UPPER:    PUSH   H   ; keep TOS: rpushd pops it back
01AB   87                     ADD   A   
01AC   6F                     MOV   L,A   
01AD   26 07                  MVI   H,LETPAGE   ; HL -> cell
01AF   50                     MOV   D,B   
01B0   59                     MOV   E,C   ; DE = the return address
01B1   4E                     MOV   C,M   
01B2   23                     INX   H   
01B3   46                     MOV   B,M   ; IP = the word's body, and fall into rpushd
01B4                             ; rpushd: push DE on the return stack, then pop TOS off the data stack and
01B4                             ; go on. Every push of the return stack ends here: for a word call the cell
01B4                             ; popped is the TOS that upper parked; for "(" and "{" it is the cell under
01B4                             ; the one that was used up.
01B4                RPUSHD:      
01B4                          IF   CHECKED   
01B4   CD 37 04               CALL   chkbrk   ; Ctrl-C is checked at every word call, block
01B7                          ENDIF      ;   entry, loop-back and "{"
01B7   2A 34 07               LHLD   RSP   
01BA   2B                     DCX   H   
01BB   72                     MOV   M,D   
01BC   2B                     DCX   H   
01BD   73                     MOV   M,E   
01BE   22 34 07               SHLD   RSP   
01C1   E1                     POP   H   
01C2   F7                     RST   6   
01C3                             ; ---- machine code: the grave -----------------------------------------------
01C3                             ; "`" plus a hex digit loads bytes: ( addr -- addr' ). Pairs of hex digits
01C3                             ; are stored from addr until a non-hex character; then a RET (C9h) is
01C3                             ; written and its address is left. An odd last digit is consumed and dropped.
01C3                             ; "`" plus anything else calls the machine code at TOS: ( addr -- ). The
01C3                             ; code is entered by CALL with the data stack above the return address; it
01C3                             ; must keep BC, and on return the top cell becomes the new TOS.
01C3   CD EE 03     H_GRAVE:   CALL   hexc   
01C6   D2 2B 01               JNC   exec   
01C9   87           HX1:      ADD   A   
01CA   87                     ADD   A   
01CB   87                     ADD   A   
01CC   87                     ADD   A   
01CD   57                     MOV   D,A   ; the high digit
01CE   CD EE 03               CALL   hexc   
01D1   D2 E0 01               JNC   hx2   ; odd digit: consumed and dropped
01D4   B2                     ORA   D   
01D5                          IF   CHECKED   
01D5   CD 44 04               CALL   chkst   
01D8                          ENDIF      
01D8   77                     MOV   M,A   
01D9   23                     INX   H   
01DA   CD EE 03               CALL   hexc   
01DD   DA C9 01               JC   hx1   
01E0                HX2:         
01E0                          IF   CHECKED   
01E0   CD 44 04               CALL   chkst   
01E3                          ENDIF      
01E3   36 C9                  MVI   M,0C9h   
01E5   F7                     RST   6   
01E6                             ; ---- where the two pages meet ----------------------------------------------
01E6                             ; The first page ends somewhere among the next four handlers, ] \ [ @ (they
01E6                             ; are in falling code order for this), and where exactly differs between the
01E6                             ; builds: NPG1 follows. Every handler below these four must start in the
01E6                             ; second page, and every one above in the first; chktab.py checks both.
01E6                             ; "]" returns: pop an address and jump to it. TOS is parked on the stack
01E6                             ; while rpop uses HL, and the drop at the end brings it back.
01E6   E5           H_RET:    PUSH   H   
01E7   CF           RET2:     RST   1   
01E8   44                     MOV   B,H   
01E9   4D                     MOV   C,L   
01EA   DF                     RST   3   
01EB                             ; "\" ( flag -- ): true skips to the next ")" or "]" at this level; ")"
01EB                             ; drops the block start, "]" returns. No closer at all ends the program.
01EB                             ; The flag stays in HL as the spent cell that rdrop and ret2 drop.
01EB   7C           H_BREAK:   MOV   A,H   
01EC   B5                     ORA   L   
01ED   CA DE 02               JZ   h_drop   ; false: just drop the flag
01F0   CD BA 03               CALL   skip   
01F3   B7                     ORA   A   ; skip returns 0 for ")"
01F4   C2 E7 01               JNZ   ret2   
01F7   C3 06 01               JMP   rdrop   
01FA                             ; "[" followed by a letter stores the body"s address in that letter"s cell:
01FA                             ; uppercase is a word, lowercase a variable. Followed by a space it pushes
01FA                             ; the body"s address instead. Either way it then skips to the matching "]'.
01FA                             ; (The unchecked build takes anything that is not a letter as the space; the
01FA                             ; checked build stops on it.)
01FA   0A           H_DEF:    LDAX   B   
01FB   03                     INX   B   
01FC   D6 41                  SUI   "A"   ; a letter gives 0-25 or 32-57: lowercase
01FE   5F                     MOV   E,A   ;   lands 64 bytes up
01FF   E6 DF                  ANI   0DFh   ; fold case
0201   FE 1A                  CPI   26   
0203   D2 13 02               JNC   def2   ; not a letter
0206   7B                     MOV   A,E   
0207   87                     ADD   A   
0208   5F                     MOV   E,A   
0209   16 07                  MVI   D,LETPAGE   ; DE -> cell
020B   79                     MOV   A,C   
020C   12                     STAX   D   
020D   1C                     INR   E   
020E   78                     MOV   A,B   
020F   12                     STAX   D   
0210   C3 1C 02               JMP   skipnx   
0213                DEF2:        
0213                          IF   CHECKED   
0213   7B                     MOV   A,E   
0214   FE DF                  CPI   " "-"A"+256   
0216   C2 6D 04               JNZ   e_brack   ; anything but a letter or a space
0219                          ENDIF      
0219   E5                     PUSH   H   ; an anonymous block: push its address
021A   60                     MOV   H,B   
021B   69                     MOV   L,C   
021C   CD BA 03     SKIPNX:   CALL   skip   
021F   F7                     RST   6   
0220   5E           H_FETCH:   MOV   E,M   ; "@"
0221   23                     INX   H   
0222   56                     MOV   D,M   
0223   EB                     XCHG      
0224   F7                     RST   6   
0225                             ; =============================================================================
0225                             ;  Handlers that must start in the image's second page.
0225                             ;  "?" is the last (with "," inside it in the unchecked build), so its long
0225                             ;  tail may run past that page.
0225                             ; =============================================================================
0225                             ; ---- flow control ----------------------------------------------------------
0225                             ; "(" ( flag -- ): true pushes the block start and enters; false skips to
0225                             ; the matching ")".
0225   7C           H_OPEN:   MOV   A,H   
0226   B5                     ORA   L   
0227   E1                     POP   H   
0228   CA 1C 02               JZ   skipnx   
022B   E5                     PUSH   H   ; (rpushd pops it again)
022C   50                     MOV   D,B   
022D   59                     MOV   E,C   ; the block starts at the IP
022E   C3 B4 01               JMP   rpushd   
0231                             ; ")" ( flag -- ): true jumps back to the block start (and keeps it); false
0231                             ; drops it and carries on.
0231   7C           H_CLOSE:   MOV   A,H   
0232   B5                     ORA   L   
0233   CA 06 01               JZ   rdrop   
0236   CF                     RST   1   ; pop the block start ...
0237   44                     MOV   B,H   
0238   4D                     MOV   C,L   ; ... jump to it ...
0239   EB                     XCHG      
023A   C3 B4 01               JMP   rpushd   ; ... and push it back (which drops the flag)
023D                             ; ---- arithmetic and logic: ( NOS TOS -- result ) ---------------------------
023D                             ; "-" has two jobs: directly before a digit it starts a negative number.
023D   0A           H_SUB:    LDAX   B   
023E   D6 30                  SUI   "0"   
0240   FE 0A                  CPI   10   
0242   DA 59 03               JC   negnum   
0245   E7                     RST   4   ; a - b = a + (-b): fall into "+"
0246   D1           H_ADD:    POP   D   
0247   19                     DAD   D   
0248   F7                     RST   6   
0249   D1           H_AND:    POP   D   
024A   7C                     MOV   A,H   
024B   A2                     ANA   D   
024C   67                     MOV   H,A   
024D   7D                     MOV   A,L   
024E   A3                     ANA   E   
024F   6F                     MOV   L,A   
0250   F7                     RST   6   
0251                             ; Signed compares. Both are "DE < HL" for the right pair: > swaps the two
0251                             ; cells first (XTHL), < doesn't. There is no overflow flag, so the signed
0251                             ; answer is the unsigned borrow of DE - HL, flipped when the signs differ.
0251                             ; SBB A turns a carry into -1 or 0 with no branch.
0251   E3           H_GT:     XTHL      ; a > b  is  b < a
0252   D1           H_LT:     POP   D   ; a < b: DE = a, HL = b
0253   7B                     MOV   A,E   
0254   95                     SUB   L   
0255   7A                     MOV   A,D   
0256   9C                     SBB   H   
0257   9F                     SBB   A   ; A = -1 if DE < HL unsigned
0258   6F                     MOV   L,A   
0259   7C                     MOV   A,H   
025A   AA                     XRA   D   
025B   17                     RAL      ; carry = the signs differ
025C   9F                     SBB   A   
025D   AD                     XRA   L   ; flip when they do
025E   67                     MOV   H,A   
025F   6F                     MOV   L,A   
0260   F7                     RST   6   
0261   D1           H_EQ:     POP   D   
0262   7D                     MOV   A,L   
0263   AB                     XRA   E   
0264   6F                     MOV   L,A   
0265   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0266   AA                     XRA   D   
0267   B5                     ORA   L   ; zero if equal
0268   D6 01                  SUI   1   ; carry only for zero
026A   9F                     SBB   A   
026B   67                     MOV   H,A   
026C   6F                     MOV   L,A   
026D   F7                     RST   6   
026E                             ; "*": shift-and-add on the multiplier's low bit, so it stops as soon as the
026E                             ; multiplier is used up; only the low 16 bits are kept.
026E   D1           H_MUL:    POP   D   ; DE = multiplicand
026F   C5                     PUSH   B   
0270   44                     MOV   B,H   
0271   4D                     MOV   C,L   ; BC = multiplier
0272   21 00 00               LXI   H,0   
0275   78           MUL1:     MOV   A,B   
0276   B7                     ORA   A   ; clear carry
0277   1F                     RAR      
0278   47                     MOV   B,A   
0279   79                     MOV   A,C   
027A   1F                     RAR      
027B   4F                     MOV   C,A   ; BC >> 1, carry = the bit shifted out
027C   D2 80 02               JNC   mul2   
027F   19                     DAD   D   
0280   EB           MUL2:     XCHG      
0281   29                     DAD   H   ; multiplicand << 1
0282   EB                     XCHG      
0283   78                     MOV   A,B   
0284   B1                     ORA   C   
0285   C2 75 02               JNZ   mul1   
0288   C1                     POP   B   
0289   F7                     RST   6   
028A                             ; "/" ( a b -- q r ): the remainder is on top. Truncates toward zero; r takes
028A                             ; a's sign. Divide |a| by |b|, then q gets the sign of a XOR b and r the sign
028A                             ; of a. Dividing by zero is not checked: it returns two cells of no meaning.
028A   D1           H_DIV:    POP   D   ; DE = a, HL = b
028B   C5                     PUSH   B   
028C   7A                     MOV   A,D   
028D   B7                     ORA   A   
028E   F5                     PUSH   PSW   ; S flag = sign of a (for r)
028F   AC                     XRA   H   
0290   F5                     PUSH   PSW   ; S flag = sign of q
0291   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0292   B7                     ORA   A   
0293   FC 20 01               CM   neg16   ; HL = |b|
0296   EB                     XCHG      
0297   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0298   B7                     ORA   A   
0299   FC 20 01               CM   neg16   ; HL = |a|, DE = |b|
029C   CD 76 03               CALL   udiv   ; HL = q, BC = r
029F   F1                     POP   PSW   
02A0   FC 20 01               CM   neg16   ; q's sign
02A3   EB                     XCHG      ; DE = q
02A4   60                     MOV   H,B   
02A5   69                     MOV   L,C   ; HL = r
02A6   F1                     POP   PSW   
02A7   FC 20 01               CM   neg16   ; r's sign
02AA   C1                     POP   B   
02AB   D5                     PUSH   D   ; q under r
02AC   F7                     RST   6   
02AD                             ; ---- stack and storage -----------------------------------------------------
02AD   E5           H_DUP:    PUSH   H   ; ":"
02AE   F7                     RST   6   
02AF   E3           H_SWAP:   XTHL      ; "%"
02B0   F7                     RST   6   
02B1   D1           H_STORE:   POP   D   ; "!" ( n addr -- )
02B2                          IF   CHECKED   
02B2   23                     INX   H   ; both bytes must be in the program's space
02B3   CD 44 04               CALL   chkst   
02B6   2B                     DCX   H   
02B7                          ENDIF      
02B7   73                     MOV   M,E   
02B8   23                     INX   H   
02B9   72                     MOV   M,D   
02BA   DF                     RST   3   
02BB   D1           H_CSTORE:   POP   D   ; "." ( c addr -- )
02BC                          IF   CHECKED   
02BC   CD 44 04               CALL   chkst   
02BF                          ENDIF      
02BF   73                     MOV   M,E   
02C0   DF                     RST   3   
02C1                             ; ---- console ---------------------------------------------------------------
02C1                             ; 22h pushes the address of the text after it and skips the string.
02C1   E5           H_STR:    PUSH   H   
02C2   60                     MOV   H,B   
02C3   69                     MOV   L,C   
02C4   CD E1 03               CALL   skipstr   
02C7   F7                     RST   6   
02C8                             ; "$" prints the string at TOS, decoding escapes: "/" plus a character
02C8                             ; clears that character"s bit 6 (/M is CR, /` is space; "/" and ""' have no
02C8                             ; bit 6, so // and /" give themselves).
02C8   7E           H_PRINT:   MOV   A,M   
02C9   23                     INX   H   
02CA   FE 22                  CPI   22h   
02CC   CA DE 02               JZ   h_drop   
02CF   FE 2F                  CPI   "/"   
02D1   C2 D8 02               JNZ   pr1   
02D4   7E                     MOV   A,M   
02D5   23                     INX   H   
02D6   E6 BF                  ANI   0BFh   
02D8   EF           PR1:      RST   5   
02D9   C3 C8 02               JMP   h_print   
02DC   7D           H_EMIT:   MOV   A,L   ; "'"
02DD   EF                     RST   5   
02DE   DF           H_DROP:   RST   3   ; ";" is this one byte
02DF                             ; "#" prints TOS as a signed decimal number, with no space after it.
02DF   7C           H_NUM:    MOV   A,H   
02E0   B7                     ORA   A   
02E1   F2 E8 02               JP   num1   
02E4   3E 2D                  MVI   A,"-"   
02E6   EF                     RST   5   
02E7   E7                     RST   4   
02E8   C5           NUM1:     PUSH   B   
02E9   CD A8 03               CALL   pdec   
02EC   C1                     POP   B   
02ED   DF                     RST   3   
02EE                          IF   CHECKED   ; (the checked build has no room to start ","
02EE   6E           H_CFETCH:   MOV   L,M   ;   as late as the unchecked one does: see
02EF   26 00                  MVI   H,0   ;   the end of "?")
02F1   F7                     RST   6   
02F2                          ENDIF      
02F2                             ; "?" ( n -- c ) or ( -n -- addr )
02F2                             ;   n > 0: wait about n ms for a key; 0 if none came
02F2                             ;   n = 0: wait for a key
02F2                             ;   n < 0: read a line of at most -n characters, with echo. The buffer
02F2                             ;          holds 127 characters and the CR: a bigger count is taken as 127.
02F2   7C           H_KEY:    MOV   A,H   
02F3   B7                     ORA   A   
02F4   FA 12 03               JM   line   
02F7   1E 28        KT1:      MVI   E,MSLOOP   ; one millisecond, roughly
02F9   CD 01 04     KT2:      CALL   getk   
02FC   C2 0E 03               JNZ   kt3   
02FF   1D                     DCR   E   
0300   C2 F9 02               JNZ   kt2   
0303   7C                     MOV   A,H   ; 0? never counts down: it waits
0304   B5                     ORA   L   
0305   CA F7 02               JZ   kt1   
0308   2B                     DCX   H   
0309   7C                     MOV   A,H   
030A   B5                     ORA   L   
030B   C2 F7 02               JNZ   kt1   ; A = 0 if the time ran out
030E                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              DB   0FEh   ; (CPI: steps over the one byte of ",")
                    H_CFETCH:   MOV   A,M   ; "," shares "?"s ending: A becomes TOS
030E                          ENDIF      
030E   6F           KT3:      MOV   L,A   
030F   26 00                  MVI   H,0   
0311   F7                     RST   6   
0312                          IF   CPM   
0312                             ; CP/M: BDOS 10 does the editing (the spec allows the platform's
0312                             ; own line editor). It doesn't store the CR, so it is added here.
0312   11 7F 00     LINE:     LXI   D,127   ; TOS is minus the count: adding 127 carries
0315   19                     DAD   D   ;   only for 1 to 127, and leaves 127 - count
0316   9F                     SBB   A   
0317   A5                     ANA   L   ; (0 for a count that is too big)
0318   EE 7F                  XRI   127   ; A = the count, 127 at most
031A   32 7E 07               STA   LBHDR   
031D   C5                     PUSH   B   
031E   11 7E 07               LXI   D,LBHDR   
0321   0E 0A                  MVI   C,10   
0323   CD 05 00               CALL   BDOS   
0326   C1                     POP   B   
0327   21 7F 07               LXI   H,LBHDR+1   
032A   7E                     MOV   A,M   ; the count typed (0-127)
032B   2C                     INR   L   ; HL = LINEBUF, whose low byte is 80h:
032C   85                     ADD   L   ;   adding the count to L can't carry
032D   6F                     MOV   L,A   
032E   36 0D                  MVI   M,13   
0330   2E 80                  MVI   L,LINEBUF & 0FFh   
0332   F7                     RST   6   
0333                          ENDIF      
0333                          IFN   CPM   
                                 ; Generic: Backspace takes the last character back (and is echoed as
                                 ; it is), CR ends (stored, not echoed), every other key is stored and
                                 ; echoed until the line is full. The line buffer starts at offset 80h
                                 ; of its page, so L alone is the place in the line: D holds the L of
                                 ; a full line.
                    LINE:     LXI   D,127   ; TOS is minus the count: adding 127 carries
                              DAD   D   ;   only for 1 to 127, and leaves 127 - count
                              SBB   A   
                              ANA   L   ; (0 for a count that is too big)
                              CMA      
                              MOV   D,A   ; D = the L of a full line: 80h + count, FFh
                                 ;   at most
                              LXI   H,LINEBUF   
                    LN2:      CALL   getk   
                              JZ   ln2   
                              CPI   13   
                              JZ   ln5   
                              CPI   8   
                              JZ   ln4   
                              MOV   E,A   
                              MOV   A,L   
                              CMP   D   
                              JZ   ln2   ; full
                              MOV   M,E   
                              INR   L   
                              MOV   A,E   
                    LN3:      RST   5   
                              JMP   ln2   
                    LN4:      DCR   L   ; Backspace: one back, and echo it,
                              JM   ln3   ;   unless the line was empty (L left the
                              INR   L   ;   upper half of the page)
                              JMP   ln2   
                    LN5:      MOV   M,A   ; the CR
                              MVI   L,LINEBUF & 0FFh   
                              RST   6   
0333                          ENDIF      
0333                             ; =============================================================================
0333                             ;  Dispatch table: the low byte of each handler's address, in code order.
0333                             ;  It must not cross a page (the dispatcher only adds to its low byte).
0333                             ; =============================================================================
0333                             ; The handlers of the first NPG1 characters start in the image's second page.
0333                             ; ] \ [ @ sit where the two pages meet, and which side each lands on
0333                             ; differs between the builds, so the count is worked out here.
0333                             ; (One division to a line: asm80 only rounds down when it stores a value.)
0333                PGRET:    EQU   (h_ret-BASE)/256   ; 0 = first page, 1 = second
0333                PGBRK:    EQU   (h_break-BASE)/256   
0333                PGDEF:    EQU   (h_def-BASE)/256   
0333                PGFET:    EQU   (h_fetch-BASE)/256   
0333                NPG1:     EQU   21 + PGFET + PGDEF + PGBRK + PGRET   
0333   B1           PTAB:     DB   h_store & 0FFh   ; !
0334   C1                     DB   h_str & 0FFh   ; "
0335   DF                     DB   h_num & 0FFh   ; #
0336   C8                     DB   h_print & 0FFh   ; $
0337   AF                     DB   h_swap & 0FFh   ; %
0338   49                     DB   h_and & 0FFh   ; &
0339   DC                     DB   h_emit & 0FFh   ; '
033A   25                     DB   h_open & 0FFh   ; (
033B   31                     DB   h_close & 0FFh   ; )
033C   6E                     DB   h_mul & 0FFh   ; *
033D   46                     DB   h_add & 0FFh   ; +
033E   EE                     DB   h_cfetch & 0FFh   ; ,
033F   3D                     DB   h_sub & 0FFh   ; -
0340   BB                     DB   h_cstore & 0FFh   ; .
0341   8A                     DB   h_div & 0FFh   ; /
0342   AD                     DB   h_dup & 0FFh   ; :
0343   DE                     DB   h_drop & 0FFh   ; ;
0344   52                     DB   h_lt & 0FFh   ; <
0345   61                     DB   h_eq & 0FFh   ; =
0346   51                     DB   h_gt & 0FFh   ; >
0347   F2                     DB   h_key & 0FFh   ; ?
0348   20                     DB   h_fetch & 0FFh   ; @
0349   FA                     DB   h_def & 0FFh   ; [
034A   EB                     DB   h_break & 0FFh   ; \
034B   E6                     DB   h_ret & 0FFh   ; ]
034C   83                     DB   h_xor & 0FFh   ; ^
034D   96                     DB   h_alloc & 0FFh   ; _
034E   C3                     DB   h_grave & 0FFh   ; `
034F   14                     DB   h_tor & 0FFh   ; {
0350   8B                     DB   h_or & 0FFh   ; |
0351   1D                     DB   h_fromr & 0FFh   ; }
0352   93                     DB   h_not & 0FFh   ; ~
0353                PTABEND:      
0353                             ; =============================================================================
0353                             ;  Routines (no handler starts past this point)
0353                             ; =============================================================================
0353                             ; Digits: step back onto the first digit and read the whole number.
0353   E5           DIGIT:    PUSH   H   
0354   0B                     DCX   B   
0355   CD 5F 03               CALL   rdnum   
0358   F7                     RST   6   
0359                             ; negnum: "-" directly before a digit: read the number, negate it.
0359   E5           NEGNUM:   PUSH   H   
035A   CD 5F 03               CALL   rdnum   
035D   E7                     RST   4   
035E   F7                     RST   6   
035F                             ; rdnum: read decimal digits at IP into HL; IP is left on the first
035F                             ; non-digit. Values wrap at 16 bits, as the spec says.
035F   21 00 00     RDNUM:    LXI   H,0   
0362   0A           RDN1:     LDAX   B   
0363   D6 30                  SUI   "0"   
0365   FE 0A                  CPI   10   
0367   D0                     RNC      
0368   03                     INX   B   
0369   54                     MOV   D,H   
036A   5D                     MOV   E,L   
036B   29                     DAD   H   
036C   29                     DAD   H   
036D   19                     DAD   D   
036E   29                     DAD   H   ; HL * 10
036F   5F                     MOV   E,A   
0370   16 00                  MVI   D,0   
0372   19                     DAD   D   
0373   C3 62 03               JMP   rdn1   
0376                             ; udiv: unsigned HL / DE (DE <= 8000h). Returns HL = quotient, BC = remainder.
0376                             ; Uses A, BC; the caller saves the IP. HL holds the dividend and, as its bits
0376                             ; leave at the top, the quotient bits arrive at the bottom. The loop counter
0376                             ; lives on the stack, since A is busy with the shifts.
0376                             ; Dividing by 2 is one shift (the spec wants that fast).
0376   01 00 00     UDIV:     LXI   B,0   
0379   7B                     MOV   A,E   
037A   EE 02                  XRI   2   
037C   B2                     ORA   D   
037D   C2 8A 03               JNZ   udv0   
0380   B4                     ORA   H   ; A was 0, and the carry is clear
0381   1F                     RAR      
0382   67                     MOV   H,A   
0383   7D                     MOV   A,L   
0384   1F                     RAR      
0385   6F                     MOV   L,A   ; the quotient
0386   78                     MOV   A,B   
0387   17                     RAL      
0388   4F                     MOV   C,A   ; the remainder: the bit that fell out
0389   C9                     RET      
038A   3E 10        UDV0:     MVI   A,16   
038C   F5                     PUSH   PSW   
038D   29           UDV1:     DAD   H   ; next dividend bit into the carry
038E   79                     MOV   A,C   
038F   17                     RAL      
0390   4F                     MOV   C,A   
0391   78                     MOV   A,B   
0392   17                     RAL      
0393   47                     MOV   B,A   ; BC = BC*2 + bit
0394   79                     MOV   A,C   
0395   93                     SUB   E   
0396   78                     MOV   A,B   
0397   9A                     SBB   D   ; carry if BC < DE
0398   DA A0 03               JC   udv2   
039B   47                     MOV   B,A   ; BC - DE (high byte; A holds it)
039C   79                     MOV   A,C   
039D   93                     SUB   E   
039E   4F                     MOV   C,A   
039F   2C                     INR   L   ; quotient bit
03A0   F1           UDV2:     POP   PSW   
03A1   3D                     DCR   A   
03A2   F5                     PUSH   PSW   
03A3   C2 8D 03               JNZ   udv1   
03A6   F1                     POP   PSW   
03A7   C9                     RET      
03A8                             ; pdec: print HL unsigned, by recursion on HL / 10 (the stack holds digits).
03A8                             ; Uses BC.
03A8   11 0A 00     PDEC:     LXI   D,10   
03AB   CD 76 03               CALL   udiv   ; HL = HL / 10, C = the last digit
03AE   79                     MOV   A,C   
03AF   F5                     PUSH   PSW   
03B0   7C                     MOV   A,H   
03B1   B5                     ORA   L   
03B2   C4 A8 03               CNZ   pdec   
03B5   F1                     POP   PSW   
03B6   C6 30                  ADI   "0"   
03B8   EF                     RST   5   
03B9   C9                     RET      
03BA                             ; skip: read past text to the closer at this level, and return A = 0 if it
03BA                             ; was ")" and 2 if it was "]". Brackets of both kinds count together;
03BA                             ; strings are stepped over whole. A NUL first ends the program (for "\" with
03BA                             ; no closer; anything else that runs into the NUL had unbalanced brackets
03BA                             ; anyway). D counts the open levels, starting at 1 for the one we are in:
03BA                             ; skip sets it to 0 and falls through the INR that an opener comes back to.
03BA   16 00        SKIP:     MVI   D,0   
03BC   14           SK3:      INR   D   ; an opener: one deeper
03BD   0A           SK1:      LDAX   B   
03BE   03                     INX   B   
03BF   B7                     ORA   A   
03C0   CA 80 01               JZ   endprog   
03C3   FE 22                  CPI   22h   
03C5   CC E1 03               CZ   skipstr   ; leaves A = 22h, which matches nothing below
03C8   D6 28                  SUI   "("   
03CA   CA BC 03               JZ   sk3   
03CD   3D                     DCR   A   ; ")"
03CE   CA DB 03               JZ   sk4   
03D1   D6 32                  SUI   "["-")"   
03D3   CA BC 03               JZ   sk3   
03D6   FE 02                  CPI   "]"-"["   
03D8   C2 BD 03               JNZ   sk1   
03DB   15           SK4:      DCR   D   
03DC   C8                     RZ      ; the closer at this level
03DD   C3 BD 03               JMP   sk1   
03E0                             ; skipstr: IP is inside a string; step past its closing quote. "/" escapes
03E0                             ; the next character, so "/"" does not end it. Leaves A = 22h.
03E0   03           SS0:      INX   B   
03E1   0A           SKIPSTR:   LDAX   B   
03E2   03                     INX   B   
03E3   FE 2F                  CPI   "/"   
03E5   CA E0 03               JZ   ss0   
03E8   FE 22                  CPI   22h   
03EA   C2 E1 03               JNZ   skipstr   
03ED   C9                     RET      
03EE                             ; hexc: if the character at IP is a hex digit (0-9, A-F, a-f), step over it
03EE                             ; and return its value in A with the carry set; otherwise leave the IP and
03EE                             ; return with the carry clear.
03EE   0A           HEXC:     LDAX   B   
03EF   D6 30                  SUI   "0"   
03F1   FE 0A                  CPI   10   
03F3   DA FF 03               JC   hc1   
03F6   E6 DF                  ANI   0DFh   
03F8   D6 11                  SUI   11h   
03FA   FE 06                  CPI   6   
03FC   D0                     RNC      
03FD   D6 F6                  SUI   0F6h   ; + 10, and sets the carry
03FF   03           HC1:      INX   B   
0400   C9                     RET      
0401                             ; =============================================================================
0401                             ;  Console layer: getk returns a waiting key in A (zero flag clear), or
0401                             ;  A = 0 with the zero flag set when none is waiting. putc (RST 5) prints A.
0401                             ;  Both keep BC, DE and HL. In the generic build they are the host's KEY and
0401                             ;  CONOUT routines themselves.
0401                             ; =============================================================================
0401                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-CHECKED)   
                    GETK:     EQU   KEY   ; the host's routine does the whole job
0401                          ENDIF      
0401                          IF   CHECKED   
0401   E5           GETK:     PUSH   H   ; a key held back by the break check goes
0402   21 36 07               LXI   H,KEYBUF   ;   first, and is taken out of the buffer
0405   7E                     MOV   A,M   
0406   36 00                  MVI   M,0   
0408   E1                     POP   H   
0409   B7                     ORA   A   
040A   C0                     RNZ      
040B                          ENDIF      
040B                          IF   (1-CPM)*CHECKED   
                              JMP   KEY   
040B                          ENDIF      
040B                          IF   CPM*(1-CHECKED)   
                    GETK:        
040B                          ENDIF      
040B                          IF   CPM   
040B   3E FF                  MVI   A,0FFh   ; BDOS 6 with E = FFh: a key, or 0
040D                             ; putc: BDOS 6 for every character. BDOS 2 would check for ^S while
040D                             ; printing and could swallow a key that BDOS 6 then never sees.
040D   C5           PUTC:     PUSH   B   
040E   D5                     PUSH   D   
040F   E5                     PUSH   H   
0410   5F                     MOV   E,A   
0411   0E 06                  MVI   C,6   
0413   CD 05 00               CALL   BDOS   
0416   E1                     POP   H   
0417   D1                     POP   D   
0418   C1                     POP   B   
0419   B7                     ORA   A   ; (for getk)
041A   C9                     RET      
041B                          ENDIF      
041B                             ; =============================================================================
041B                             ;  Checked build: the checks and the error report
041B                             ; =============================================================================
041B                          IF   CHECKED   
041B                             ; chkstk: both stacks are checked once per character, not in every handler.
041B                             ; Each stack lives in one page, so it has overrun exactly when the pointer's
041B                             ; high byte has left that page. Errors are caught one cell late at most; the
041B                             ; page below each stack is a guard band. (The call itself is on the data
041B                             ; stack, but in the same page whenever the stack is in range.)
041B   EB           CHKSTK:   XCHG      ; DE = TOS (HL is needed for the pointers)
041C   21 00 00               LXI   H,0   
041F   39                     DAD   SP   
0420   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0421   FE 06                  CPI   DSPAGE   
0423   C2 64 04               JNZ   e_stack   
0426   2A 34 07               LHLD   RSP   ; the return stack: in its page, and not
0429   7D                     MOV   A,L   ;   above its empty position (an underflow
042A   FE E1                  CPI   RSTOP&0FFh+1   ;   would stay inside the page, in the
042C   D2 67 04               JNC   e_rstack   ;   guard band)
042F   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0430   FE 05                  CPI   RSPAGE   
0432   C2 67 04               JNZ   e_rstack   
0435   EB                     XCHG      ; TOS back
0436   C9                     RET      
0437                             ; chkbrk: a waiting key is read now; Ctrl-C stops the program, anything
0437                             ; else is held for the next "?". Keeps BC, DE, HL.
0437   CD 01 04     CHKBRK:   CALL   getk   
043A   C8                     RZ      
043B   FE 03                  CPI   3   
043D   CA 6A 04               JZ   e_break   
0440   32 36 07               STA   KEYBUF   
0443   C9                     RET      
0444                             ; chkst: stop unless HL is in the program's own space: from the letter page
0444                             ; up to the heap limit (the OS, or HEAPLIM), so the interpreter's stacks and
0444                             ; whatever lies above the limit are safe. Memory above the heap top but
0444                             ; below the limit is the program's own: Tiny BASIC keeps its lines there.
0444                             ; Keeps every register.
0444   F5           CHKST:    PUSH   PSW   
0445   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0446   FE 07                  CPI   LETPAGE   
0448   DA 61 04               JC   e_store   
044B                          ENDIF      
044B                          IF   CHECKED*(1-CPM)   
                              CPI   HEAPLIM   
                              JNC   e_store   
044B                          ENDIF      
044B                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
044B   3A 07 00               LDA   0007h   ; the BDOS page is the heap limit
044E   3D                     DCR   A   
044F   BC                     CMP   H   
0450   DA 61 04               JC   e_store   
0453                          ENDIF      
0453                          IF   CHECKED   
0453   F1                     POP   PSW   
0454   C9                     RET      
0455                             ; chkhp: stop if working out the new heap top carried (a negative count
0455                             ; wraps: too big), or if the new top in HL is not below the limit page.
0455   DA 5E 04     CHKHP:    JC   e_heap   
0458                          ENDIF      
0458                          IF   CHECKED*(1-CPM)   
                              MOV   A,H   
                              CPI   HEAPLIM   
                              RC      
0458                          ENDIF      
0458                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
0458   3A 07 00               LDA   0007h   
045B   3D                     DCR   A   
045C   BC                     CMP   H   
045D   D0                     RNC      
045E                          ENDIF      
045E                          IF   CHECKED   
045E                             ; Error entries. Each loads its letter and then hides the next entry inside
045E                             ; a 3-byte LXI H (the 21h), so they all fall through to `error`.
045E   3E 48        E_HEAP:   MVI   A,"H"   ; heap past the limit
0460   21                     DB   21h   
0461   3E 57        E_STORE:   MVI   A,"W"   ; write outside the program's space
0463   21                     DB   21h   
0464   3E 53        E_STACK:   MVI   A,"S"   ; data stack over or under
0466   21                     DB   21h   
0467   3E 52        E_RSTACK:   MVI   A,"R"   ; return stack over or under
0469   21                     DB   21h   
046A   3E 42        E_BREAK:   MVI   A,"B"   ; Ctrl-C
046C   21                     DB   21h   
046D   3E 44        E_BRACK:   MVI   A,"D"   ; bad character after [
046F                             ; error: print the letter in A, " @ " and the offset in the program of the
046F                             ; character just read, then end. For example: S @ 245
046F   31 FE 06     ERROR:    LXI   SP,DSTOP   ; the stacks may be wrecked: start clean
0472   EF                     RST   5   
0473   3E 20                  MVI   A," "   
0475   EF                     RST   5   
0476   3E 40                  MVI   A,"@"   
0478   EF                     RST   5   
0479   3E 20                  MVI   A," "   
047B   EF                     RST   5   
047C   21 FF F7               LXI   H,(0-PROG-1)&0FFFFh   ; minus the address of the character
047F   09                     DAD   B   ;   just read: HL = its offset
0480   CD A8 03               CALL   pdec   
0483   C3 80 01               JMP   endprog   
0486                          ENDIF      
0486                             ; =============================================================================
0486                             ;  Startup
0486                             ; =============================================================================
0486                START:       
0486                          IF   CPM   
0486                             ; CP/M: the RAM pages follow the image; the heap may grow to the BDOS
0486   21 08 01               LXI   H,vecs   ; the RST routines go down into page zero
0489   11 08 00               LXI   D,0008h   
048C   06 2C                  MVI   B,vecend-vecs   
048E   7E           CPY:      MOV   A,M   
048F   12                     STAX   D   
0490   23                     INX   H   
0491   13                     INX   D   
0492   05                     DCR   B   
0493   C2 8E 04               JNZ   cpy   
0496   11 5C 00               LXI   D,005Ch   ; open the file named on the command line
0499   0E 0F                  MVI   C,15   ; (no such file: the first read fails too,
049B   CD 05 00               CALL   BDOS   ;   and the program is empty)
049E   11 00 08               LXI   D,PROG   
04A1   D5           LD1:      PUSH   D   
04A2   0E 1A                  MVI   C,26   ; set the DMA address
04A4   CD 05 00               CALL   BDOS   
04A7   11 5C 00               LXI   D,005Ch   
04AA   0E 14                  MVI   C,20   ; read the next 128 bytes
04AC   CD 05 00               CALL   BDOS   
04AF   E1                     POP   H   ; HL = the address this record went to
04B0   B7                     ORA   A   
04B1   C2 BC 04               JNZ   ld2   
04B4   11 80 00               LXI   D,128   
04B7   19                     DAD   D   
04B8   EB                     XCHG      
04B9   C3 A1 04               JMP   ld1   
04BC   36 00        LD2:      MVI   M,0   ; the end of the file counts as NUL
04BE   23                     INX   H   ; the heap starts after it
04BF                          ENDIF      
04BF                          IFN   CPM   
                              LXI   H,PROG   ; the heap starts after the program's NUL
                    FNUL:     MOV   A,M   
                              INX   H   
                              ORA   A   
                              JNZ   fnul   
04BF                          ENDIF      
04BF   22 7C 07               SHLD   HEAP   
04C2   21 E0 05               LXI   H,RSTOP   ; the return stack is empty
04C5   22 34 07               SHLD   RSP   
04C8                          IF   CHECKED   
04C8   AF                     XRA   A   
04C9   32 36 07               STA   KEYBUF   ; no key held back
04CC                          ENDIF      
04CC   01 00 08               LXI   B,PROG   ; the IP
04CF   F7                     RST   6   ; (its return address is thrown away)
04D0                          IF   CPM   
04D0                             ; RAM pages, after the image
04D0                RSPAGE:   EQU   (imgend + 255) / 256   
04D0                DSPAGE:   EQU   RSPAGE + 1   
04D0                LETPAGE:   EQU   RSPAGE + 2   
04D0                PROG:     EQU   LETPAGE*256 + 256   
04D0                          ENDIF      
04D0                IMGEND:      


